(a) Nothing in this Code or the ordinance adopting this Code shall affect or be construed to repeal or otherwise affect the validity of any of the following:
(1) Any ordinance or resolution promising or guaranteeing the payment of money by or for the city or authorizing the issuance of any bonds of the city or any evidence of the city's indebtedness or any contract or obligation assumed by the city;
(2) Any ordinance or resolution granting any franchise or right;
(3) Any ordinance or resolution appropriating funds, levying or imposing taxes or relating to an annual budget;
(4) Any ordinance or resolution relating to salaries, compensation or bonds of city officers and employees or members of city boards or commissions or to compensation or pay plans or classification plans for such officers or employees;
(5) Any ordinance or resolution authorizing, providing for or otherwise relating to any specific public improvement or making any assessment;
(6) Any ordinance or resolution annexing territory of the city or otherwise altering the boundaries of the city;
(7) Any zoning ordinance or amendments thereto, and any ordinance establishing a board of zoning appeals, board of architectural review, or planning commission, including joint commissions;
(8) Any ordinance or resolution dedicating or accepting any subdivision plat or providing for subdivision regulations;
(9) Any contract or obligation assumed by the city;
(10) Any ordinance or resolution establishing and prescribing employment and personnel policies and procedures;
(11) Any ordinance or resolution dedicating, naming, establishing, locating, relocating, closing, opening, widening, paving, vacating, etc., any street or public way in the city;
(12) Any ordinance or resolution establishing and prescribing the street grades of any street in the city;
(13) Any appropriation ordinance;
(14) The administrative ordinances or resolutions of the city not in conflict or inconsistent with the provisions of this Code;
(15) Any ordinance or resolution of agreement with another political subdivision;
(16) Any ordinance or regulation prescribing traffic regulations for specific locations concerning through streets, parking limitations, parking prohibitions, one-way traffic, limitations on loads of vehicles or loading zones, not in conflict or inconsistent with this Code;
(17) Any ordinance or resolution establishing the amount of a fee, fine, rate or charge imposed by the provisions of this Code, or any ordinance contained therein or amendatory thereto;
(18) Any ordinance or resolution adopted for purposes which have been consummated;
(19) Any ordinance or resolution which is temporary, although general in effect, or special, although permanent in effect; or
(20) Any ordinance or resolution establishing, accepting or amending a zoning map, thoroughfare map, or thoroughfare plan.
(b) All such ordinances are hereby recognized as continuing in full force and effect to the same extent as if set out at length in this Code.
(Code 1986, § 1-7)

